    "instructions": "omr/instructions/42055-1-1.pdf (one book, 552 pages: the mine truck is pages 1-46, steps 1-72; the excavator is pages 47-541; its functions are drawn on pages 542-545). The model file holds both, the truck standing beside the excavator",
    "functions": [
      {
        "does": "The orange switch on the battery box, at the back end of the counterweight boom, switches the Power Functions XL motor on, one way.",
        "source": "book: page 542 (the inset: the switch pushed one way)",
        "control": "p3369 58119",
        "note": "the motor is p3153 58121; everything below marked as motor-driven needs it running"
      },
      {
        "does": "The XL motor, beside the gearbox on the counterweight boom, drives a gearbox whose three red knobs, on top, choose what it works; with the middle knob pulled back (towards the knob's lower arrow) it turns the bucket wheel and runs the conveyor belts: the boom's belt carrying the spoil from the wheel to the middle, and the discharge belt carrying it out over the back.",
        "source": "book: page 543, function A (middle knob back, the other two at N: the wheel turns and both belts run); inferred from the model: which catch is each knob",
        "control": "p3250 6641",
        "moves": [
          "p2426 42055 - 24120 against p2535 42055 - 55615",
          "p2339 57520 against p2535 42055 - 55615",
          "p1869 57520"
        ],
        "stays": [
          "p418 64178",
          "p1599 42055 - 18938"
        ],
        "note": "motor-driven. The middle knob is taken as the catch p3250 6641, at x 40 between the other two. The wheel's teeth are the four ring quarters 24121 (p2429, p2459, p2478, p2479) and its buckets 24120"
      },
      {
        "does": "With the middle knob back, the right knob, pushed forward or back, slews the whole upper works round on the crawler base one way or the other, while the wheel and belts keep running: two worms turn on a big ring gear made of four quarters on the base.",
        "source": "book: page 543, function B; inferred from the model: the worms p1330 4716 and the ring quarters p810-p813 24121, and which catch is the right knob (seen from behind the counterweight)",
        "control": "p3241 6641",
        "moves": [
          "p418 64178 against p1175 18939"
        ],
        "note": "motor-driven; the slew is drawn as the base turning against the upper works, which the model makes the frame"
      },
      {
        "does": "With the middle knob pushed forward, the left knob, pushed forward or back, drives the excavator forward or back on its two crawler tracks; the wheel and belts stop. The drive goes down a shaft through the middle of the slewing turntable to an axle carrying both tracks' sprockets, so the two tracks always run together.",
        "source": "book: page 543, function C (middle knob forward, left knob up or down); inferred from the model: the shaft p488 32073 down the turntable's middle and the sprocket axle with p911 and p1018 57520, and which catch is the left knob",
        "control": "p3259 6641",
        "first": [
          {
            "control": "p3250 6641",
            "by": -1
          }
        ],
        "moves": [
          "p911 57520",
