      },
      {
        "does": "The red lever at the back, pushed down (lock), slides a driving ring that ties the discharge belt's turntable to the crawler base, so when the upper works slews the discharge belt stays aimed where it was, over the truck.",
        "source": "book: page 545, function E (the lever down and locked, the right knob worked: the upper works turns and the discharge belt stays over the truck); page 544 (E labelled); inferred: through which parts",
        "control": "p1678 6641",
