        "note": "check with the slew: with this lever locked and the right knob worked, p1599 42055 - 18938 should keep its heading against p418 64178 while the upper works turns"
      },
      {
        "does": "The black gear at the foot of the tower, used as a crank, raises and lowers the bucket wheel boom: a cross shaft with bevel gears turns two linear actuators, one each side, that push the boom up about its pivot, carrying the counterweight boom, motor and gearbox with it.",
        "source": "book: page 545, function F; page 544 (F labelled); inferred from the model: the cross shaft p1501 and the actuators",
